390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (In modern defence systems, surveillance and threat detection are essential for maintaining national security and protecting military personnel. A major challenge for defence forces is identifying enemies or objects hidden using camouflage, which blend into environments like forests or deserts and evade traditional systems.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (While advanced Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) can detect these threats, standard AI models require massive computing power, quickly draining the batteries of small edge devices and surveillance drones. To overcome this, our project introduces an ultra-low-power system using Spiking Neural Networks \(SNNs\). Deployed directly on an edge device, it analyzes unusual patterns and textures to detect camouflaged threats in real-time, improving battlefield awareness without the heavy power cost.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
